noo a 6-point edge, averaging to a narrow Republican margin. Scott's durable personal brand and incumbency in a D-leaning state, plus markets pricing him near 85%, justify keeping him favored despite the unusually tight polling.", "watch": "Whether subsequent polls confirm the UNH result showing Janoo ahead or revert to Scott's historical double-digit margins.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Phil Scott (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Vermont's governor race pairs one of the country's most popular Republican incumbents, Phil Scott, against Democrat Amanda Janoo in a state that leans 17 points Democratic at the presidential level. Scott has repeatedly outrun his party's brand, but 2026 polling suggests this race is closer than any of his previous contests. A late-September Vermont Public survey shows him up 10 points, while a UNH survey released the same week shows Janoo narrowly ahead, citing partisan headwinds. Betting markets still price Scott at roughly 82-85%, and most expert raters call the race Safe or Solid Republican, though one rates it Likely Republican. The campaign has centered on Vermont's healthcare crisis, where the candidates offer contrasting plans. Scott remains favored on his incumbency and personal appeal, but the polling disagreement leaves real uncertainty about the final margin.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2101, "margin": -4.77}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0165, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0219, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0312, "margin": -10.8}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2344, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2363, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2599, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2631, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2569, "margin": -4.0}]}